<% if (typeof clarityProjectId !== 'undefined' && clarityProjectId && !(typeof noClarity !== 'undefined' && noClarity)) { %><script nonce="<%= nonce %>">
  (function(c,l,a,r,i,t,y){
    c[a]=c[a]||function(){(c[a].q=c[a].q||[]).push(arguments)};
    t=l.createElement(r);t.async=1;t.src="https://www.clarity.ms/tag/"+i;
    y=l.getElementsByTagName(r)[0];y.parentNode.insertBefore(t,y);
  })(window, document, "clarity", "script", "<%= clarityProjectId %>");
  (function () {
    var paid = false;
    try {
      var q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
      if (q.has('msclkid') || /^(bing|microsoft)$/i.test(q.get('utm_source') || '')) {
        sessionStorage.removeItem('arrPaidGoogle');
      } else if (q.has('gclid') || q.has('gbraid') || q.has('wbraid') ||
          ((q.get('utm_source') || '').toLowerCase() === 'google' && /^(cpc|ppc)$/i.test(q.get('utm_medium') || ''))) {
        sessionStorage.setItem('arrPaidGoogle', '1');
      }
      paid = sessionStorage.getItem('arrPaidGoogle') === '1';
    } catch (e) {}
    if (paid) window.clarity('set', 'traffic', 'google_ads');
  })();
</script>
<% } %><%# Microsoft Clarity (session recordings and heatmaps), 01/10/2026.
    Microsoft's own snippet with one change, nonce="..." on the inline
    script, for the same CSP reason as the Google tag beside it. It renders
    only when CLARITY_PROJECT_ID is set on the service (server.js validates
    the id and puts it in app.locals, so no view has to pass it). Included
    from google-tag.ejs so it reaches exactly the pages the Google tag
    reaches: every public page, never Scott or the Workspace. Clarity masks
    form inputs by default, and the Privacy page describes it.

    Paid Google Ads visits are tagged traffic = google_ads (12/10/2026), so
    recordings can be filtered to them under Filters, Custom tags. Leads-
    Search-1 and Ready to Sell carry only Google's click id (auto-tagging,
    no UTM suffix), so Clarity's own Source/Medium filters cannot see them.
    The flag lives in sessionStorage so every page of that visit is tagged,
    and only the label is sent: never the click id itself.

    Fix brief of 12/10/2026, item 4: a visitor who arrives from a Microsoft
    advert (msclkid, or utm_source bing/microsoft: the same rule as
    microsoft-uet.ejs) loses the flag, so the rest of that visit is not
    labelled a Google Ads visit. Clarity keeps any label it was already sent
    on earlier pages; this stops it being sent again. And the staff login
    page sets noClarity (res.locals, routes/auth.js), so it is never
    recorded at all. %>
